    <h2>2. Informational content, not medical advice</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing on this site is intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease or condition,
      and nothing here should be read as medical or health advice. Incense is a fragrance, ritual, and
      craft practice — not a treatment, a sleep aid, an anxiety remedy, or a substitute for care.
      If you have a medical concern, a sleep disorder, a respiratory condition, or any question about
      your health, consult a qualified healthcare professional. Do not use this content to make health
      decisions, and do not ingest, inhale, or otherwise administer any botanical material based on
      traditional-medicine descriptions without professional guidance.
    </p>
    <p>
      References to "health" or "wellness" on this site describe how incense is used culturally — in
      ritual, meditation, or household fragrance — not a claim about what it does to your body.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Traditional use vs modern evidence</h2>
    <p>
      Where materials are described in traditional or historical terms — for example, classical Chinese
      materia-medica language such as 行气止痛 ("to move qi and relieve pain") or 温中 ("to warm the
      middle") — that is <strong>traditional knowledge, recorded as history and culture</strong>, not
      modern clinical evidence. Traditional uses are never presented as proven health effects, and they
      are never offered as a reason to use a material medicinally.
    </p>
    <p>
      LanDeng separates three distinct kinds of statement and labels them consistently throughout the
      site: (a) <strong>historical record</strong> — what classical texts said, reported as history;
      (b) <strong>scientific finding</strong> — what modern research has or has not established, with
      its source and evidence tier; and (c) <strong>trade terminology</strong> — the vocabulary of the
      incense industry, labeled as such. An uncertain claim is marked uncertain. This separation is
      described in our <a href="/blog/landeng-editorial-methodology/">editorial methodology</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Not professional advice of any other kind</h2>
    <p>
      The site is also not legal, financial, investment, or tax advice. Information about sourcing,
